      "writtenOn": "2022-06-22T04:26:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "tbh motivation behind the change in \"_test.go\" was to remove the dependency of \"fmt\". I noticed that the vendored code does not contain test files. \\\n\nShould I revert the change, or use \"hex.EncodeToString\"?\n\nWhile writing Go, What is preferred in this use case? Irrespective of whether it is a normal package or a _test.go file?",
      "parentUuid": "86477fff_424056de",
      "revId": "4f36628a4a57fdf585bc875ec99240dd73af8bed",
