      "writtenOn": "2022-06-22T21:25:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I started this thread primarily to point out that the property of not importing \"fmt\" doesn\u0027t apply to this package\u0027s tests (in case it causes confusion for future code readers), and it sounds like you\u0027ve considered it now.\n\nI think both Sprintf(\"%x\") and hex.EncodeToString are good choices in this context. hex.EncodeToString reads well here since the const name is \u0027expectedHex\u0027, so it seems okay to keep it as is.",
